    "timeMinutes": null,
    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "In the given diagram, the two shapes which are reflections of each other in the line $y=x$ are:",
    "image": "qimages/samf/junior-2009-r1/q07.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "P and Q"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "P and S"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "R and S"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "Q and R"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "P and R"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Swap the coordinates",
        "body": "Reflection in $y=x$ swaps $x$ and $y$: a shape in the upper left with $x<y$ goes to a shape with $x>y$ below the line. So the only candidates are the shapes above the line (P, S) paired with those below it (Q, R). A vertical shape reflects into a horizontal one.\n\nP and Q match each other (the slanted corner of P reflects to the slanted corner of Q). R has its slant pointing down and to the right, but S's slant would reflect to a slant pointing the other way, so R and S are not reflections.\n\n**Answer: (A) P and Q**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "geometry"
    ],
    "difficulty": 2,
    "duplicateOf": null,
    "reviewNote": null
  },
  {
