    "grade": "8-9",
    "points": 5,
    "timeMinutes": null,
    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "Points $P$, $Q$, $R$ and $S$ are marked on the sides of square $ABCD$ so that each side is divided in the ratio 2 : 1, and therefore $PQRS$ is a square. The ratio of the area of $PQRS$ to the area of $ABCD$ is:",
    "image": "qimages/samf/junior-2009-r1/q09.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt6}9$"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "$\\frac49$"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt5}9$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$\\frac59$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$\\frac23$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Pythagoras",
        "body": "Let the side of $ABCD$ be 3, so each side is cut into 2 and 1. A side of $PQRS$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle with legs 2 and 1, so its square is $4+1=5$. The ratio of areas is $\\frac59$.\n\n**Answer: (D) $\\frac59$**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Subtract corner triangles",
        "body": "Each of the four corner triangles has area $\\frac12\\cdot2\\cdot1=1$, so $PQRS$ has area $9-4=5$ out of 9.\n\n**Answer: (D) $\\frac59$**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "geometry"
    ],
    "difficulty": 2,
    "duplicateOf": null,
    "reviewNote": null
  },
