    "grade": "8-9",
    "points": 5,
    "timeMinutes": null,
    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "$1287a45b$ is an 8-digit number, where $a$ and $b$ are not zero. The number is divisible by 18. The maximum possible difference between $a$ and $b$ is:",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "4"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "5"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "6"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "7"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "8"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Divisibility by 2 and 9",
        "body": "Divisible by 18 means even and divisible by 9. So $b$ is even and the digit sum $1+2+8+7+4+5+a+b=27+a+b$ is a multiple of 9, i.e. $a+b\\in\\{9,18\\}$. $a+b=18$ needs $a=b=9$, not even. So $a+b=9$ with $b\\in\\{2,4,6,8\\}$: $(a,b)=(7,2),(5,4),(3,6),(1,8)$ with differences $5,1,3,7$. The maximum is 7.\n\n**Answer: (D) 7**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "number-theory"
    ],
    "difficulty": 3,
    "duplicateOf": null,
    "reviewNote": null
  },
