    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "A beadworker is threading beads onto a straight wire; he has four green beads and two red beads and will use them all. The number of different arrangements he can make is:",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "13"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "14"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "15"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "16"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "17"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Choose the red positions",
        "body": "An arrangement is determined by which 2 of the 6 positions hold red beads: $\\binom62=\\frac{6\\cdot5}2=15$.\n\n**Answer: (C) 15**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Count systematically",
        "body": "If the first red bead is in position 1, the second can be in 5 places; if in position 2, 4 places; and so on: $5+4+3+2+1=15$.\n\n**Answer: (C) 15**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
