    "prompt": "A small wheel of radius 2 cm rolls around the circumference of a larger wheel of radius 5 cm without slipping. The small wheel has a black spot on it at the point marked $P$. If the small wheel starts rolling from the position shown in the diagram, how many times will the point $P$ touch the circumference of the larger wheel before $P$ comes back to its original position (and the small circle comes back to its original position)?",
    "image": "qimages/samf/junior-2009-r1/q15.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "2"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "3"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "4"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "5"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "6"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Match the circumferences",
        "body": "The large wheel has circumference $10\\pi$ and the small wheel $4\\pi$, a ratio of $5:2$. After a whole number of laps $L$ the small wheel has turned through $\\frac{10\\pi L}{4\\pi}=\\frac{5L}2$ rolls, and everything is back in place only when this is a whole number: $L=2$, giving 5 rolls.\n\nIn each roll of the small wheel the spot touches the large wheel once, so $P$ touches it 5 times.\n\n**Answer: (D) 5**"
      }
    ],
