        "key": "B",
        "text": "$20^\\circ$"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$25^\\circ$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$30^\\circ$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$35^\\circ$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Chase angles",
        "body": "Let $\\angle D=x$. Since $EC=ED$, $\\angle ECD=x$ and the exterior angle $\\angle AEC=2x$. Since $CA=CE$, $\\angle EAC=\\angle AEC=2x$.\n\nTriangle $ABC$ is equilateral so $\\angle ACB=60^\\circ$, which is an exterior angle of triangle $ACD$: $60^\\circ=\\angle CAD+\\angle D=2x+x$. So $x=20^\\circ$.\n\n**Answer: (B) $20^\\circ$**"
      }
    ],
