    "prompt": "The number of positive integers $n$ for which $3n-6$ is divisible by $n-1$ is:",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "0"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "1"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "2"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "3"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "4"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Divide out",
        "body": "$\\frac{3n-6}{n-1}=3-\\frac3{n-1}$. This is an integer exactly when $n-1$ divides 3. We need $n-1\\ne0$, and $n-1\\in\\{1,3\\}$ (the negative divisors $-1,-3$ would give $n\\le0$), so $n=2$ or $n=4$.\n\nCheck: $n=2$: $0$ is divisible by 1. $n=4$: $6$ is divisible by 3.\n\n**Answer: (C) 2**"
      }
    ],
